#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119500 :question/id #uuid "d2cb7f5f-ad04-5e04-b2da-0f9b555442a3" :question/math-academy-id "e-10974" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the line with equation $y=5+3x$ in $\\mathbb{R}^2.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $L$ contains the zero-vector\n\nII. $L$ is closed under vector addition\n\nIII. $L$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIV. $L$ is **not** a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^2$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0 \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{0}$ for any vector $\\mathbf{v}$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $L$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]} = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ 5 + 3 x\\end{array} \\right]}, \\qquad x \\in \\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is false. The coordinates of the zero-vector do not satisfy the equation $y=5+3x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5+3x \\\\ (0) & =5+3(0) \\\\ 0 & =5\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Let, for example, $\\mathbf{a}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ 5\\end{array} \\right]}$ and $\\mathbf{b}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 1 \\\\ 2\\end{array} \\right]}$ from $L.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0+(-1) \\\\ 5+2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nHowever, ${\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 1 \\\\ 7\\end{array} \\right]} \\notin L$ since substituting the coordinates into the equation $y=5+3x$ gives the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5+3x \\\\ 7 & =5+3(-1) \\\\ 7 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $\\mathbf{0} \\not\\in L,$ this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since statements II and III are false, $L$ is *not* a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119501 :question/id #uuid "d0d76105-c49e-5cf8-af57-bd74989e895b" :question/math-academy-id "e-10977" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the line in $\\mathbb{R}^3$ that passes through the points $(1,2,2)$ and $(2,1,1).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $L$ contains the zero-vector\n\nII. $L$ is closed under vector addition\n\nIII. $L$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIV. $L$ is **not** a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^3$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0 \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{0}$ for any vector $\\mathbf{v}$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is false. The direction vector of the line $L$ is \n$$\n\\mathbf{d}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{array} \\right]} -   {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{array} \\right]}  = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ - 1 \\\\ - 1\\end{array} \\right]} .\n$$\nThis means that the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in\\mathbb R,$ and the corresponding Cartesian equation is \n\n$$\n{x-1}=\\dfrac{y-2}{-1}=\\dfrac{z-2}{-1}.\n$$\n\nBut this line does not pass through the origin since \n\n$$\n{(0)-1}\\neq\\dfrac{(0)-2}{-1}=\\dfrac{(0)-2}{-1}.  \\quad {\\color{red}\\times}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Let's consider the vectors $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ from $L$ (the position vectors of the given points). Then,\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{array} \\right]} + {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{array} \\right]} = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$\nHowever, the point $(3,3,3)$ does not belong to $L$ since\n\n$$\n{(3)-1}\\neq\\dfrac{(3)-2}{-1}=\\dfrac{(3)-2}{-1}. \\quad {\\color{red}\\times}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $\\mathbf{0} \\not\\in L,$ this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since statements II and III are false, $L$ is *not* a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119502 :question/id #uuid "d2199de1-4bfe-5589-95dd-f9bb7c339437" :question/math-academy-id "e-10980" :question/problem "Let $\\Pi$ be the plane with equation $x+4y-3z=2$ in $\\mathbb{R}^3.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $\\Pi$ contains the zero-vector\n\nII. $\\Pi$ is closed under vector addition\n\nIII. $\\Pi$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIV. $\\Pi$ is **not** a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^3$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0 \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{0}$ for any vector $\\mathbf{v}$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $\\Pi$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{array} \\right]} = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}2 - 4 y + 3 z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{array} \\right]}, \\qquad y,z \\in \\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is false. The plane does not pass through the origin since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+4y-3z & =2 \\\\ (0)+4(0)-3(0) & =2 \\\\ 0 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Let's consider $\\mathbf{a}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{array} \\right]} \\in \\Pi$ and $\\mathbf{b}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{array} \\right]} \\in \\Pi.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2+1 \\\\ 0+1 \\\\ 0+1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ does not belong to $\\Pi$ since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+4y-3z & =2 \\\\ (3)+4(1)-3(1) & =2 \\\\ 4 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $\\mathbf{0} \\not\\in \\Pi,$ this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since statements II and III are false, $\\Pi$ is *not* a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120145 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90bf2615-f44c-5a92-b7f7-16b4105c8c76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477151} {:answer/id #uuid "ca27e4e3-8bca-5871-9395-a6380f99cd94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca27e4e3-8bca-5871-9395-a6380f99cd94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477152} :answer-field/id #uuid "27cef8a9-5b30-53f7-9387-8d249e05a639" :answer-field/key "$L$ contains the zero-vector" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477545} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4aca2503-832b-575e-b56c-b125e1b5c5d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477153} {:answer/id #uuid "e6f4c934-20cf-5792-9fd6-4e318ffcf52c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477154}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6f4c934-20cf-5792-9fd6-4e318ffcf52c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477154} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9674e23-7a9d-5e22-aede-cfbab89607f8" :answer-field/key "$L$ is closed under vector addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477546} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bfe5c36-5e7c-5bd5-87a1-4069378067df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477155} {:answer/id #uuid "f9f2d338-3f3e-5490-a9bc-b39400a94b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9f2d338-3f3e-5490-a9bc-b39400a94b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477156} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd7028b-5925-58dd-9e69-36d0f34bb338" :answer-field/key "$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477547} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dad4bcf4-7bb7-58ca-92ea-68aab62ad28a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477157} {:answer/id #uuid "a05fa06f-95fd-5a6f-8b50-f72c429bbdcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a05fa06f-95fd-5a6f-8b50-f72c429bbdcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477158} :answer-field/id #uuid "2211ec51-ee76-5442-bf6d-ce7726af963f" :answer-field/key "$L$ is a subspace of ${R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "44d1d34b-4b40-5331-8b03-073462e9a684" :question/math-academy-id "q-155956" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the line with equation $x=2y$ in ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $L$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement “$L$ contains the zero-vector” is true. The coordinates of the zero-vector satisfy the equation $x=2y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2y \\\\ (0) & =2(0) \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is closed under vector addition” is true. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}2a \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}\\in L$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}2b \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}\\in L.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}2a \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2b \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2a+2b \\\\ a+b\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2(a+b) \\\\ a+b\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $x=2y.$ Therefore, $a+b\\in L.$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is true. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}2a \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}\\in L$ and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k\\cdot a & =k\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2a \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2ka \\\\ ka\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $x=2y.$ Therefore, $k\\cdot a\\in L.$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is a subspace of ${R}^{2}$” is true. Since statements “$L$ is closed under vector addition” and “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” are true, $L$ must be a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"All the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24252954-787b-5287-ada3-c3c084627cbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459561} {:answer/id #uuid "0ea7f730-2ff2-5228-b790-8f8914e58843" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24252954-787b-5287-ada3-c3c084627cbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459561} :answer-field/id #uuid "558fdbad-eec9-50d1-9396-20fe7193cb95" :answer-field/key "$L$ contains the zero-vector" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460647} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f04425c-7df1-58ad-b1e6-f2932fcc8dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459563} {:answer/id #uuid "dacc05fc-1ec1-5c2a-8d1d-3483419a8522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f04425c-7df1-58ad-b1e6-f2932fcc8dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459563} :answer-field/id #uuid "8497150c-19f4-5c2a-ae83-13740f506308" :answer-field/key "$L$ is closed under vector addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460648} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22251dfe-d083-5dc0-aef6-975964d95330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459565} {:answer/id #uuid "148689b1-11a7-55ba-b407-5c7f94bd335b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22251dfe-d083-5dc0-aef6-975964d95330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459565} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3f6846b-3415-5ec5-80cb-0595a3ec6235" :answer-field/key "$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460649} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0514bb18-c8aa-5a5a-a02c-b2ade3e4b60b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459567} {:answer/id #uuid "079aa3e4-f3eb-5f67-9f8d-9697c3429fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "079aa3e4-f3eb-5f67-9f8d-9697c3429fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459568} :answer-field/id #uuid "f181aeb8-c359-5992-b7c4-2c5057fd3737" :answer-field/key "$L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460650}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3b679935-b7fe-5b87-9b05-95735d1a350e" :question/math-academy-id "q-155957" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the line in ${R}^{3}$ that passes through the points $(-2,2,-2)$ and $(3,-4,2).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement “$L$ contains the zero-vector” is false. The direction vector of the line $L$ is \n\n$$\nd=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis means that the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in R,$ and the corresponding Cartesian equation is \n\n$$\n\\frac{x+2}{5}=\\frac{y-2}{-6}=\\frac{z+2}{4}.\n$$\n\nBut this line does not pass through the origin since \n\n$$\n\\frac{(0)+2}{5}\\ne \\frac{(0)-2}{-6}\\ne \\frac{(0)+2}{4}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is closed under vector addition” is false. Let's consider the vectors $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ from $L$ (the position vectors of the given points). Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHowever, the point $(1,-2,0)$ does not belong to $L$ since\n\n$$\n\\frac{(1)+2}{5}\\ne \\frac{(-2)-2}{-6}\\ne \\frac{(0)+2}{4}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. Since $0\\notin L,$ this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$” is true. Since statements “$L$ is closed under vector addition” and “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” are false, $L$ is *not* a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120150 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e4aa7af-8e65-56ef-819b-139ea1e8f1e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448422} {:answer/id #uuid "2065cab8-cb21-54d6-94e1-b4b41f0a9f2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e4aa7af-8e65-56ef-819b-139ea1e8f1e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448422} :answer-field/id #uuid "10b6ea84-6376-54ab-96c2-52e2850b8611" :answer-field/key "$L$ contains the zero-vector" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449251} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba4c529a-16f2-5ba1-a671-c872c0a87c26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448424} {:answer/id #uuid "5136518b-8276-5038-9702-9cadb0a02eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba4c529a-16f2-5ba1-a671-c872c0a87c26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448424} :answer-field/id #uuid "94f2baf9-c041-5c30-bc69-006f9e288c0d" :answer-field/key "$L$ is closed under vector addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449252} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b720d1d-4786-52f6-b181-142bfc0915cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448426} {:answer/id #uuid "976d669d-a25a-5e0d-8370-ea5f89cf2984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b720d1d-4786-52f6-b181-142bfc0915cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448426} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9656039-a18e-523c-a419-cc089ff54e48" :answer-field/key "$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449253} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73990243-f849-5436-9398-edc0b840c742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448428} {:answer/id #uuid "806954d4-5596-58d9-a021-a4e661ee44cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "806954d4-5596-58d9-a021-a4e661ee44cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448429} :answer-field/id #uuid "4482a4af-af62-5f1a-a13f-0a50c8a9c069" :answer-field/key "$L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2d2b6331-122d-5166-a305-241f7f5b32d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-156607" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the line with equation $y=1-2x$ in ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $L$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ 1-2x\\end{bmatrix},\\,x\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement “$L$ contains the zero-vector” is false. The coordinates of the zero-vector do not satisfy the equation $y=1-2x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =1-2x \\\\ (0) & =1-2(0) \\\\ 0 & =1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is closed under vector addition” is false. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ from $L.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0+1 \\\\ 1-1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nHowever, $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\notin L$ since substituting the coordinates into the equation, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =1-2x \\\\ (0) & =1-2(1) \\\\ 0 & =-1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. Since $0\\notin L,$ this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{2}$” is true. Since statements “$L$ is closed under vector addition” and “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” are false, $L$ is *not* a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{2}$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120151 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34ac7fa6-59a2-56c7-9df0-60e6f9d373a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448430} {:answer/id #uuid "05d3173c-d6b0-53b5-b89c-0ce5e9739205" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05d3173c-d6b0-53b5-b89c-0ce5e9739205" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448431} :answer-field/id #uuid "536d01eb-316b-5f78-85cc-6db641672f4e" :answer-field/key "$L$ contains the zero-vector" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449255} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca54fc57-c37e-51a6-a86f-a516fb08af34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448432} {:answer/id #uuid "dfdcb3c8-29fb-582c-af97-98c3b894e5e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfdcb3c8-29fb-582c-af97-98c3b894e5e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448433} :answer-field/id #uuid "e10c661f-1bbc-5bcf-8d4f-c1cfe52baa32" :answer-field/key "$L$ is closed under vector addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449256} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1438a80e-a496-5dd2-92bf-5b533c7b0cab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448434} {:answer/id #uuid "fa25c559-a416-5989-a7de-2ccfe3aaa0af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa25c559-a416-5989-a7de-2ccfe3aaa0af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448435} :answer-field/id #uuid "42431b57-7a25-535b-b215-21a57dd08e92" :answer-field/key "$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449257} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bdae2ec-697d-519c-aca1-c162479973d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448436} {:answer/id #uuid "741b5375-4601-52f5-8731-edbe3e16c480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bdae2ec-697d-519c-aca1-c162479973d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448436} :answer-field/id #uuid "349d2e5e-d6cf-5d91-adb1-200683782dcc" :answer-field/key "$L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449258}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fe544997-b5f0-5f74-9a6d-c604c1790f93" :question/math-academy-id "q-156679" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the line in ${R}^{3}$ that passes through the points $(0,0,0)$ and $(1,-1,1).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nFirst, note that the direction vector of the line $L$ is \n\n$$\nd=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis means that the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ -t \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in R,$ and the corresponding Cartesian equation is \n\n$$\nx=-y=z.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement “$L$ contains the zero-vector” is true. Indeed, from the definition of $L$ we have that the point $(0,0,0)$ is in $L.$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is closed under vector addition” is true. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ -a \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}\\in L$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}b \\\\ -b \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}\\in L.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ -a \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}b \\\\ -b \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a+b \\\\ -a+(-b) \\\\ a+b\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a+b \\\\ -(a+b) \\\\ a+b\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the conditions $x=-y=z.$ Therefore, $a+b\\in L.$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is true. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ -a \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}\\in L$ and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k\\cdot a & =k\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ -a \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}ka \\\\ k(-a) \\\\ ka\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}ka \\\\ -(ka) \\\\ ka\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the conditions $x=-y=z.$ Therefore, $k\\cdot a\\in L.$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$” is false. Since statements “$L$ is closed under vector addition” and “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” are true, $L$ is a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$L$ contains the zero-vector”; “$L$ is closed under vector addition”; “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120152 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d725758f-8f09-58e8-a2b8-2c73f5b76c7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448438} {:answer/id #uuid "d4673597-a503-59f4-ba36-5ea8d99378be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d725758f-8f09-58e8-a2b8-2c73f5b76c7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448438} :answer-field/id #uuid "99cc9849-b09a-5b7e-b6bd-df791e15e7f1" :answer-field/key "$Π$ contains the zero-vector" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449259} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "576125d5-2f3a-54f6-873a-edf7ed73af90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 1759