dent :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21db992d-750b-5f63-b8be-eb9f118bb7fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464459} :answer-field/id #uuid "c505563e-02f1-5d4d-b33c-cc4b08f19956" :answer-field/key "$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465163} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f159163-fe13-514b-9d7e-7661613440a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464460} {:answer/id #uuid "6a18a431-084a-513a-9d8a-fb9bebf0735e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a18a431-084a-513a-9d8a-fb9bebf0735e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464461} :answer-field/id #uuid "e378c5aa-d7e5-580c-913c-5f05c0170396" :answer-field/key "$L$ is a subspace of ${R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465164}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5f2f3e53-cc1d-51df-ab0f-2a9380a01406" :question/math-academy-id "q-156653" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the line with equation $y=-3x$ in ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $L$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ -3x\\end{bmatrix},\\,x\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement “$L$ contains the zero-vector” is true. The coordinates of the zero-vector satisfy the equation $y=-3x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x \\\\ (0) & =-3(0) \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is closed under vector addition” is true. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ -3a\\end{bmatrix}\\in L$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}b \\\\ -3b\\end{bmatrix}\\in L.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ -3a\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}b \\\\ -3b\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a+b \\\\ (-3a)+(-3b)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a+b \\\\ -3(a+b)\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $y=-3x.$ Therefore, $a+b\\in L.$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is true. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ -3a\\end{bmatrix}\\in L$ and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k\\cdot a & =k\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ -3a\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}ka \\\\ k(-3a)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}ka \\\\ -3(ka)\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $y=-3x.$ Therefore, $k\\cdot a\\in L.$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is a subspace of ${R}^{2}$” is true. Since statements “$L$ is closed under vector addition” and “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” are true, $L$ must be a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"All the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275363 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaade65c-fd86-5a9b-8729-a4c2c4ccca8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449716} {:answer/id #uuid "bb8