alue "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449720} :answer-field/id #uuid "579d8368-3de0-5e84-9641-f66bc5dcc737" :answer-field/key "$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450814} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fcc9c302-3722-57e5-8729-a3c5ced64e28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449722} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1945d1-4e98-5897-b692-84f26ca03545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d1945d1-4e98-5897-b692-84f26ca03545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449723} :answer-field/id #uuid "78f7c353-1833-5e2f-a1a0-90570b00960c" :answer-field/key "$L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450815}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "951ef63e-740e-55a7-b946-00aea8b9f2dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-156727" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the line in ${R}^{3}$ that passes through the points $(1,2,3)$ and $(3,2,1).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement “$L$ contains the zero-vector” is false.The direction vector of the line $L$ is \n\n$$\nd=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis means that the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in R,$ and the corresponding Cartesian equation is \n\n$$\n\\frac{x-1}{2}=\\frac{z-3}{-2},\\,y=2\n$$\n\nBut this line does not pass through the origin since the second coordinate of any point on this line satisfies\n\n$$\ny=2\\ne 0.\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is closed under vector addition” is false. Let's consider the vectors $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ from $L$ (the position vectors of the given points). Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHowever, point $(4,4,4)$ does not belong to $L$ since it does not satisfy the equation of the line. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\ny=4\\ne 2.\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. Since $0\\notin L,$ this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$” is true. Since statements “$L$ is closed under vector addition” and “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” are false, $L$ is *not* a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275364 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f9cc33e-c0c5-5b8b-9b7b-43449e48f5c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449724} {:answer/id #uuid "1ab14dcf-d31d-59b5-8499-1d27c4e784e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ab14dcf-d31d-59b5-8499-1d27c4e784e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449725} :answer-field/id #uuid "0651069d-7707-5fad-8a54-669911bd9d80" :answer-field/key "$Π$ contains the zero-vector" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450816} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14724386-89dd-54a5-ab82-72539dd3007f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449726} {:answer/id #uuid "9671fed1-1431-512a-aa76-99f0de1a0d1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9671fed1-1431-512a-aa76-99f0de1a0d1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449727} :answer-field/id #uuid "25f0248b-b483-56f2-af25-7de8977c4281" :answer-field/key "$Π$ is closed under vector addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450817} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71b5ce27-d0dd-5afe-aa3a-11d51af83877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449728} {:answer/id #uuid "87326de9-3ade-5902-87b1-b7d5f32e5699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87326de9-3ade-5902-87b1-b7d5f32e5699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449729} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3a7804f-54ea-5a31-bab1-80ae62f7f878" :answer-field/key "$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450818} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f36e98d-5226-5d6a-9092-d396e8b0bd32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449730} {:answer/id #uuid "812e04eb-ae5d-5f1c-86cc-e53391996a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f36e98d-5226-5d6a-9092-d396e8b0bd32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449730} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca03455e-a692-57a1-b149-1867333e9c39" :answer-field/key "$Π$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "36959921-7ebb-5f39-a723-592fbf72eec8" :question/math-academy-id "q-156728" :question/problem "Let $Π$ be the plane with equation $z=2x-5y$ in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $Π$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ 2x-5y\\end{bmatrix},\\,x,y\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement “$Π$ contains the zero-vector” is true. The coordinates of the zero-vector satisfy the equation $z=2x-5y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =2x-5y \\\\ (0) & =2(0)-5(0) \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is closed under vector addition” is true. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} \\\\ 2{a}_{1}-5{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2} \\\\ 2{b}_{1}-5{b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} \\\\ 2{a}_{1}-5{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2} \\\\ 2{b}_{1}-5{b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1}+{b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}+{b}_{2} \\\\ (2{a}_{1}-5{a}_{2})+(2{b}_{1}-5{b}_{2})\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1}+{b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}+{b}_{2} \\\\ 2({a}_{1}+{b}_{1})-5({a}_{2}+{b}_{2})\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $z=2x-5y.$ Therefore, $a+b\\in Π.$\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is true. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} \\\\ 2{a}_{1}-5{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π$ and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k\\cdot a & =k\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} \\\\ 2{a}_{1}-5{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}k{a}_{1} \\\\ k{a}_{2} \\\\ k(2{a}_{1}-5{a}_{2})\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}k{a}_{1} \\\\ k{a}_{2} \\\\ 2k{a}_{1}-5k{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $z=2x-5y.$ Therefore, $k\\cdot a\\in Π.$\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$” is false. Since statements “$Π$ is closed under vector addition” and “$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication” are true, the plane $Π$ must be a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$Π$ contains the zero-vector”; “$Π$ is closed under vector addition”; “$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275389 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01046d5c-be66-5485-af50-610e4296b3da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464462} {:answer/id #uuid "458500c3-bc8e-53db-b1fd-1babcc77c693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "458500c3-bc8e-53db-b1fd-1babcc77c693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464463} :answer-field/id #uuid "6445e721-c78c-5978-ba76-5ee282240995" :answer-field/key "$L$ contains the zero-vector" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465165} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "316245e9-d759-5092-aeec-617e24a8d3ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464464} {:answer/id #uuid "90a6c4a2-a537-561c-8e8d-b32bc2771c43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90a6c4a2-a537-561c-8e8d-b32bc2771c43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464465} :answer-field/id #uuid "912c383e-5b5c-5c6b-87cd-96a1c5fad059" :answer-field/key "$L$ is closed under vector addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465166} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "163e9113-cd83-544f-9f15-3790dc817a17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464466} {:answer/id #uuid "2e2d37e5-cbfd-53aa-b551-7174e4a13aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e2d37e5-cbfd-53aa-b551-7174e4a13aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464467} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6498908-c1aa-5ea8-9af1-2251407d7224" :answer-field/key "$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465167} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c7c4eb2-ae29-5692-b4cc-8046ee5a294a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464468} {:answer/id #uuid "0812da7a-a492-5ad9-b18f-72e82f3489ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c7c4eb2-ae29-5692-b4cc-8046ee5a294a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464468} :answer-field/id #uuid "f365d7ba-8f11-5723-bdf9-346c779e3361" :answer-field/key "$L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8ca63685-40ca-5dbf-8721-4e6b3a5a2913" :question/math-academy-id "q-157290" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the line with equation $2y=3x$ in ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $L$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}x\\end{bmatrix},\\,x\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement “$L$ contains the zero-vector” is true. The coordinates of the zero-vector satisfy the equation $2y=3x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y & =3x \\\\ 2(0) & =3(0) \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is closed under vector addition” is true. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}a\\end{bmatrix}\\in L$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}b \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}b\\end{bmatrix}\\in L.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}a\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}b \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}b\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a+b \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}a+\\frac{3}{2}b\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a+b \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}(a+b)\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $2y=3x.$ Therefore, $a+b\\in L.$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is true. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}a\\end{bmatrix}\\in L$ and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k\\cdot a & =k\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}a\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}ka \\\\ k(\\frac{3}{2}a)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}ka \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}(ka)\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $2y=3x.$ Therefore, $k\\cdot a\\in L.$\n\n- Statement “$L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{2}$” is false. Since statements “$L$ is closed under vector addition” and “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” are true, $L$ must be a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$L$ contains the zero-vector”; “$L$ is closed under vector addition”; “$L$ is closed under scalar multiplication” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275390 :question/answer-fields 