 ${R}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "70407f65-cb23-502b-8caa-ecb6f34e8d13" :question/math-academy-id "q-157468" :question/problem "Let $Π$ be the plane with equation $x+y-2z=3$ in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $Π$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3-y+2z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement “$Π$ contains the zero-vector” is false. The line does not pass through the origin since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y-2z & =3 \\\\ (0)+(0)-2(0) & =3 \\\\ 0 & =3\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is closed under vector addition” is false. Let's consider $a=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3+2 \\\\ 0+1 \\\\ 0+0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ does not belong to $Π$ since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y-2z & =3 \\\\ (5)+(1)-2(0) & =3 \\\\ 6 & =3\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. Since $0\\notin Π,$ this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$” is true. Since statements “$Π$ is closed under vector addition” and “$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication” are false, $L$ is *not* a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$Π$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275398 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2900a74a-fac1-586f-a04e-2815a3dc2f26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449794} {:answer/id #uuid "13f35b5c-5028-57c9-bd9e-6ef4ba2c727a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2900a74a-fac1-586f-a04e-2815a3dc2f26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449794} :answer-field/id #uuid "de8449d1-ce00-5c26-883b-bc17eb9c81f3" :answer-field/key "$Π$ contains the zero-vector" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450851} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35cebcd8-fadf-5199-8439-4aba6238d844" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449796} {:answer/id #uuid "5f6992de-e29a-536a-b737-a80805efbe27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35cebcd8-fadf-5199-8439-4aba6238d844" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449796} :answer-field/id #uuid "727b5db6-b100-5cac-8d8f-156912f74d52" :answer-field/key "$Π$ is closed under vector addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450852} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d924a78e-3b5e-5379-9576-673d66685a1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449798} {:answer/id #uuid "0c527088-f3e0-5a94-9ef2-14961fc4206c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d924a78e-3b5e-5379-9576-673d66685a1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449798} :answer-field/id #uuid "208d600e-5612-5018-b11a-382ea84fd68f" :answer-field/key "$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450853} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f5c81ef-7872-52c0-bf66-67355a054cdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449800} {:answer/id #uuid "f43ce531-2070-5602-8bda-788888c4b5f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f43ce531-2070-5602-8bda-788888c4b5f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449801} :answer-field/id #uuid "e913f2a9-5262-5ee2-b8d7-0d4401f35e05" :answer-field/key "$Π$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450854}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "39240080-5310-56c6-b798-6051cae1cac8" :question/math-academy-id "q-157469" :question/problem "Let $Π$ be the plane with equation $x-2y+z=1$ in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $Π$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+2y-z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement “$Π$ contains the zero-vector” is false. The line does not pass through the origin since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z & =1 \\\\ (0)-2(0)+(0) & =1 \\\\ 0 & =1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is closed under vector addition” is false. Let's consider $a=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+0 \\\\ 0+0 \\\\ 0+1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ does not belong to $Π$ since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z & =1 \\\\ (1)-2(0)+(1) & =1 \\\\ 2 & =1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. Since $0\\notin Π,$ this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$” is true. Since statements “$Π$ is closed under vector addition” and “$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication” are false, $L$ is *not* a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$Π$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275399 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e283f24-c3a1-59cf-9e3c-55ce9bf0a94a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464526} {:answer/id #uuid "62297675-ca20-5ed1-a25c-956c7f98abe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e283f24-c3a1-59cf-9e3c-55ce9bf0a94a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464526} :answer-field/id #uuid "febd412b-208a-57f4-a3e5-07cc980e96ea" :answer-field/key "$Π$ contains the zero-vector" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465197} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2929686-a438-5316-b4de-d0b3d0e5e45b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464528} {:answer/id #uuid "f37d4317-a9ec-5c5a-9f0b-ed6e65458994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2929686-a438-5316-b4de-d0b3d0e5e45b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464528} :answer-field/id #uuid "9702f944-1db8-518a-acb2-526219576d0e" :answer-field/key "$Π$ is closed under vector addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465198} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6be4fdbb-c7e4-5655-b045-b6f33961203b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464530}