nt :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668434} :answer-field/id #uuid "df3fa663-bb34-5c1a-b76b-24eac8329bbf" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668794}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "99eda82b-48bc-5827-9c44-f2725d46a5d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-157476" :question/problem "Let $Π$ be the plane with equation $x-2y+2z=3$ in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $Π$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3+2y-2z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement “$Π$ contains the zero-vector” is false. The line does not pass through the origin since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2y+2z & =3 \\\\ (0)-2(0)+2(0) & =3 \\\\ 0 & =3\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is closed under vector addition” is false. Let's consider $a=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3+1 \\\\ 0+0 \\\\ 0+1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ does not belong to $Π$ since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2y+2z & =3 \\\\ (4)-2(0)+2(1) & =3 \\\\ 6 & =3\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. Since $0\\notin Π,$ this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is a subspace of ${R}^{3}$” is false. Since statements “$Π$ is closed under vector addition” and “$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication” are false, $L$ is *not* a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376047 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7942ffbd-3d66-5ed9-8ea0-201f43aea547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471051} {:answer/id #uuid "5bc536b0-989f-5e1b-a40c-27c8294d07d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bc536b0-989f-5e1b-a40c-27c8294d07d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471052} :answer-field/id #uuid "674caa4c-2cad-580f-b8d9-d047ccbcd4ec" :answer-field/key "$Π$ contains the zero-vector" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472031} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c88b182-2851-5794-aaa3-47b0b8c5e656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471053} {:answer/id #uuid "47d2d62c-fba5-50f6-a3f9-d3ba572f8c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47d2d62c-fba5-50f6-a3f9-d3ba572f8c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471054} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5ce933d-5d23-5cc3-80c4-5e1381a4b4d8" :answer-field/key "$Π$ is closed under vector addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472032} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29002f03-0147-533f-93de-d3e06ac30cd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471055} {:answer/id #uuid "0ed403c6-727e-567d-8097-612517505274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ed403c6-727e-567d-8097-612517505274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471056} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddac7343-b072-5769-b1e8-e7be8f4fee5d" :answer-field/key "$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472033} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61f4501f-edca-5eac-9fc0-0d791a3d313d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471057} {:answer/id #uuid "24c6fb10-a538-5ef7-acb6-b358afac5aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24c6fb10-a538-5ef7-acb6-b358afac5aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471058} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8b22cd2-a990-590c-90c2-2600d5219d90" :answer-field/key "$Π$ is a subspace of ${R}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472034}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "77f2cd70-5c51-5abc-8136-b13970866790" :question/math-academy-id "q-156681" :question/problem "Let $Π$ be the plane with equation $z=x+y$ in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $Π$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ x+y\\end{bmatrix},\\,x,y\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement “$Π$ contains the zero-vector” is true. The coordinates of the zero-vector satisfy the equation $z=x+y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+y \\\\ (0) & =(0)+(0) \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is closed under vector addition” is true. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{1}+{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{1}+{b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{1}+{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{1}+{b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1}+{b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}+{b}_{2} \\\\ ({a}_{1}+{a}_{2})+({b}_{1}+{b}_{2})\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1}+{b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}+{b}_{2} \\\\ ({a}_{1}+{b}_{1})+({a}_{2}+{b}_{2})\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $z=x+y.$ Therefore, $a+b\\in Π.$\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is true. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{1}+{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\in Π$ and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k\\cdot a & =k\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{1}+{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}k{a}_{1} \\\\ k{a}_{2} \\\\ k({a}_{1}+{a}_{2})\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}k{a}_{1} \\\\ k{a}_{2} \\\\ k{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $z=x+y.$ Therefore, $k\\cdot a\\in Π.$\n\n- Statement “$Π$ is a subspace of ${R}^{3}$” is true. Since statements “$Π$ is closed under vector addition” and “$Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication” are true, the plane $Π$ must be a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"All the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376054 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12dfb173-85de-53de-8bbb-769e3ff393b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471059} {:answer/id #uuid "dee9be9f-4d3b-54bb-b16b-61cd95251fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12dfb173-85de-53de-8bbb-769e3ff393b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471059} :answer-field/id #uuid "98f7413f-d2af-5cef-8961-04ae15531969" :answer-field/key "$L$ contains the zero-vector" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472035} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5daac8d8-5f6f-5451-86d9-365c0f6282a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471061} {:answer/id #uuid "c23b81bd-b600-5fba-9034-aa425ea45b14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471062}] :answer-field/correc